        // Let's express the rule via the revert booleans:
        // success1 || success2 should be consistent with the value condition and timestamp condition.
        // More precisely: success1 == (amount == 10 ether) AND success2 == false
        // Because: if amount == 10 ether, first call succeeds (timestamp > 0), second call reverts (timestamp not > pastBlockTime).
        // If amount != 10 ether, both calls revert.
        // So success1 is true iff amount == 10 ether.
        // success2 is always false (either due to value mismatch or timestamp not strictly greater).
        // Also, if amount == 10 ether, the first call transfers ether out of this contract, but we don't assert on that here.
        assert(success1 == (amount == 10 ether) && success2 == false);
    }

